# Docker build context exclusions.
# Both Dockerfiles build from the repo root as context, so without this file every local
# bin/obj/node_modules tree gets shipped to the daemon — and, worse, COPY'd into the build
# stage on top of a clean restore. CI checks out fresh so it never bites there; a dev running
# `docker compose build` after a local `dotnet build` hits stale-artifact failures.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# .NET intermediates — must not leak into the SDK stage's restore/publish
**/bin
**/obj
**/artifacts
**/TestResults
**/*.user

# Node / frontend intermediates
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-ssr
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test + coverage output
**/coverage
**/coverage-frontend
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.cobertura.xml
**/.playwright-mcp

# Secrets — never bake into an image layer
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Docs and local scratch that no image needs
docs
research/data
**/*.log
**/logs
**/.DS_Store
